// Title: Potential Arbitrary Code Execution Via Node.EXE
// Sigma ID: 6640f31c-01ad-49b5-beb5-83498a5cd8bd
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2022-09-09 | Modified: 2023-02-03
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1127
// Description: Detects the execution node.exe which is shipped with multiple software such as VMware,
//   Adobe...etc. In order to execute arbitrary code. For example to establish reverse shell as seen
//   in Log4j attacks...etc
// False positives:
//   - Unlikely
// References:
//   - http://blog.talosintelligence.com/2022/09/lazarus-three-rats.html
//   - https://www.sprocketsecurity.com/resources/crossing-the-log4j-horizon-a-vulnerability-with-no-return
//   - https://www.rapid7.com/blog/post/2022/01/18/active-exploitation-of-vmware-horizon-servers/
//   - https://nodejs.org/api/cli.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_node_abuse.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (FolderPath endswith "\\node.exe" and (ProcessCommandLine contains " -e " or ProcessCommandLine contains " --eval ")) and (ProcessCommandLine contains ".exec(" and ProcessCommandLine contains "net.socket" and ProcessCommandLine contains ".connect" and ProcessCommandLine contains "child_process")
